## 2. Current Defenses

TechSecure Inc. employs multiple layers of security to defend against identified threats. The following table details our current defenses:

| Defense Mechanism               | Description                                           | Implemented Since | Responsible Entity         |
|----------------------------------|-------------------------------------------------------|-------------------|-----------------------------|
| Firewalls                        | Advanced perimeter security to filter traffic         | 2018              | IT Security Team            |
| Intrusion Detection System (IDS) | Monitors network traffic for suspicious activity      | 2019              | Network Security Team       |
| Endpoint Protection              | Antivirus and anti-malware solutions on all endpoints | 2020              | Systems Administration      |
| Security Information and Event Management (SIEM) | Real-time analysis of security alerts     | 2022              | Security Operations Center  |
| Multi-Factor Authentication (MFA)| Additional layer of security for user logins         | 2021              | Identity Management Team    |
| Employee Training                | Regular training on cybersecurity awareness           | 2020              | Human Resources Department  |

### 2.1 Relationships Between Defenses

The IT Security Team collaborates closely with the Network Security Team to ensure that firewalls and IDS work in tandem to identify and mitigate threats. The Systems Administration team ensures that endpoint protection is deployed effectively across all devices, while the Security Operations Center continuously monitors alerts generated by SIEM for a proactive response.

